  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The mission of SUMERNET PLUS aims to improve the policies and practices in the Mekong Region to support a just, inclusive and sustainable transition towards enhanced climate resilience in relevant key sectors across different levels (at sub-national, national, and regional levels) through inclusive and solution-oriented knowledge co-production (research), capacity development of researchers, application of innovations and policy engagement, while taking into account gender equality, disability and social inclusion and human rights based approach in the Mekong Region.

The following are the objectives of SUMERNET PLUS:

 1. Enhanced capacities and inclusive collaborations of Mekongs knowledge producers, policy influencers, and young professionals are needed to deliver credible research, solution-oriented knowledge co-production, policy engagement, and communications that respond to the differentiated needs of local communities, women and other marginalised groups, and local leaders in addressing climate resilience challenges.

2. Improved policy development and implementation by policymakers and practitioners that are inclusive, gender-responsive and grounded in human rights-based approach to deliver equitable climate resilience solutions in the Mekong Region.

3. Adoption of just, equitable and sustainable practices by the private sector and other stakeholders, based on inclusive evidence  from solution-oriented knowledge co-production, will contribute to climate resilience in the Mekong Region.</narrative>
  </description>
